#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:256
msgid "GEMM optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:258
msgid ""
"The GEMM kernel above is correct but does not reach the GPU's theoretical "
"peak (speed-of-light, or SoL) throughput. The recommended safe path is "
"mapped persistent GEMM: the output partition produces bounded, disjoint "
"indices, and the compiler derives the input bounds from the loops that "
"produce each index. This avoids `unsafe` and does not require making full "
"tensor dimensions const generics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:265
msgid "Approach 1: Mapped Persistent GEMM (Safe, Recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:267
msgid ""
"Mapped output partitions expose an iterator over output tile indices. The "
"indices are produced by the partition itself, so stores are bounded and "
"disjoint. The K-loop iterates `0..num_tiles(&part_x, 1)` and indexes the "
"input partitions with plain arrays; the compiler infers the same bounds from "
"the loop and the mapped components, and verifies the cross-tensor ties (for "
"example `ceil(dim(x, 1)/BK) <= ceil(dim(y, 0)/BK)`) as launch checks before "
"any GPU work. `deny_in_kernel_checks = true` turns any check that would "
"remain in the kernel into a compile error, so the body is assert-free by "
"construction:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:276
msgid ""
"#[cutile::entry(\n"
"    optimization_hints = (\n"
"        sm_120 = (num_cta_in_cga = 2,),\n"
"        sm_100 = (num_cta_in_cga = 2,),\n"
"    ),\n"
"    deny_in_kernel_checks = true,\n"
")]\n"
"fn gemm_persistent<\n"
"    T: ElementType,\n"
"    const BM: i32,\n"
"    const BN: i32,\n"
"    const BK: i32,\n"
"    const MAP_SHAPE: [i32; 2],\n"
">(\n"
"    mut z: MappedPartitionMut<T, { [BM, BN] }, MAP_SHAPE>,\n"
"    x: &Tensor<T, { [-1, -1] }>,\n"
"    y: &Tensor<T, { [-1, -1] }>,\n"
") {\n"
"    let part_x = x.partition(shape![BM, BK]);\n"
"    let part_y = y.partition(shape![BK, BN]);\n"
"\n"
"    for out_idx in z.iter_indices() {\n"
"        let (bid_m, bid_n) = out_idx.components();\n"
"\n"
"        let mut tile_z: Tile<T, { [BM, BN] }> = constant(T::ZERO, shape![BM, "
"BN]);\n"
"        for k_tile in 0i32..num_tiles(&part_x, 1) {\n"
"            let tile_x = part_x.load([bid_m, k_tile]);\n"
"            let tile_y = part_y.load([k_tile, bid_n]);\n"
"            tile_z = mma(tile_x, tile_y, tile_z);\n"
"        }\n"
"        z.store(tile_z, out_idx);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:312
msgid ""
"`with_bounds(...)`, `Dim::new(...)`, and `coord(...)` from earlier versions "
"of this kernel are deprecated since 0.3.0; see [Bounds-Check Placement](../"
"guide/bounds-check-placement.md) for the placement rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:317
msgid ""
"On the host side, `.map(...)` selects the mapped output traversal and the "
"launch grid is inferred from the mapped partition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:320
msgid ""
"let z = z.partition([BM, BN]).map([4, 1], num_tile_blocks);\n"
"let (z, _x, _y) = gemm_persistent(z, x, y)\n"
"    .generics(generics)\n"
"    .sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:327
msgid ""
"Changing the full runtime tensor dimensions does not require recompilation. "
"Only the type-level parameters, such as tile sizes and the map shape, "
"specialize the JIT compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:331
msgid ""
"See [`cutile-examples/examples/persistent_gemm.rs`](https://github.com/"
