#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:333
msgid "Approach 2: Disabling Bounds Checks (Unsafe)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:335
msgid ""
"The `#[cutile::entry()]` attribute accepts `unchecked_accesses` and "
"`optimization_hints`. Setting `unchecked_accesses = true` disables runtime "
"bounds checks on all tensor loads and stores and requires an `unsafe` entry "
"point. `optimization_hints` supplies architecture-specific tuning parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:340
msgid ""
"#[cutile::entry(\n"
"    unchecked_accesses = true,\n"
"    optimization_hints = (\n"
"        sm_120 = (num_cta_in_cga = 2, max_divisibility = 16,),\n"
"    )\n"
")]\n"
"unsafe fn gemm<T: ElementType, const BM: i32, const BN: i32, const BK: "
"i32>(\n"
"    z: &mut Tensor<T, { [BM, BN] }>,\n"
"    x: &Tensor<T, { [-1, -1] }>,\n"
"    y: &Tensor<T, { [-1, -1] }>,\n"
"    k: i32,\n"
") {\n"
"    let part_x = x.partition(shape![BM, BK]);\n"
"    let part_y = y.partition(shape![BK, BN]);\n"
"    let pid_m = program_id(0);\n"
"    let pid_n = program_id(1);\n"
"    let mut tile_z: Tile<T, { [BM, BN] }> = z.load();\n"
"    for i in 0i32..(k / BK) {\n"
"        let tile_x = part_x.load([pid_m, i]);\n"
"        let tile_y = part_y.load([i, pid_n]);\n"
"        tile_z = mma(tile_x, tile_y, tile_z);\n"
"    }\n"
"    z.store(tile_z);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:367
msgid "This version changes three parts of the kernel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:369
msgid ""
"**`unchecked_accesses = true`** removes bounds-checking overhead on every "
"`load` and `store` call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:370
msgid ""
"**`sm_120 = (num_cta_in_cga = 2, max_divisibility = 16,)`** is an "
"architecture-specific hint for Blackwell (SM 120) that groups two CTAs into "
"a CGA for better inter-SM data sharing and caps auto-inferred alignment at "
"16."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:371
msgid ""
"**`k` is passed as a runtime `i32`** rather than a const generic, so "
"changing the K dimension does not create a new compiled variant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:373
msgid ""
"The compiler still checks tile shapes, `mma` dimensions, and element types. "
"`unchecked_accesses` disables only runtime bounds checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:376
msgid "The call site must also use an `unsafe` block:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:378
msgid ""
"unsafe {\n"
"    let (z, _, _, _) = gemm(z, x, y, k as i32)\n"
"        .generics(generics)\n"
"        .sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:386
msgid ""
"See [`cutile-benchmarks/benches/gemm.rs`](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-"
"rust/blob/main/cutile-rs/cutile-benchmarks/benches/gemm.rs) for a full "
"benchmark comparing optimized and unoptimized variants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:388
msgid "Approach 3: Fully Static GEMM (Safe, Legacy)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:390
msgid ""
"The older safe performance path is to make **all** tensor dimensions static "
"const generics. When the compiler knows every dimension and the launch grid "
"at JIT time, it can prove direct `program_id(axis)` partition accesses are "
"in bounds and optimize the checks away entirely - no `unsafe` required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:395
msgid ""
"#[cutile::entry()]\n"
"fn gemm<\n"
"    E: ElementType,\n"
"    const BM: i32, const BN: i32, const BK: i32,\n"
"    const M: i32, const N: i32, const K: i32,\n"
">(\n"
"    z: &mut Tensor<E, { [BM, BN] }>,\n"
"    x: &Tensor<E, { [M, K] }>,\n"
"    y: &Tensor<E, { [K, N] }>,\n"
") {\n"
"    let part_x = x.partition(shape![BM, BK]);\n"
"    let part_y = y.partition(shape![BK, BN]);\n"
"    let mut tile_z = load_tile_mut(z);\n"
"    let pid_m = program_id(0);\n"
"    let pid_n = program_id(1);\n"
"    for i in 0i32..(K / BK) {\n"
"        let tile_x = part_x.load([pid_m, i]);\n"
"        let tile_y = part_y.load([i, pid_n]);\n"
"        tile_z = mma(tile_x, tile_y, tile_z);\n"
"    }\n"
"    z.store(tile_z);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:420
msgid "In this version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:422
msgid ""
"**`x: &Tensor<E, { [M, K] }>` and `y: &Tensor<E, { [K, N] }>`** — input "
"dimensions are fully static instead of dynamic (`-1`). The compiler sees the "
"exact shape of every tensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:423
msgid ""
"**No `unsafe`, no `unchecked_accesses`** — bounds checks are present in the "
"source but the JIT compiler proves they are redundant and eliminates them "
"during optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:424
msgid ""
"**`M`, `N`, `K` are const generics** — they must be passed via `.generics()` "
"at launch time, and every new combination creates a new compiled variant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:425
msgid ""
"**`.const_grid(grid)`** — optional. The launch grid is inferred from the "
"output partition as usual; `.const_grid()` additionally passes the grid as a "
"compile-time constant, which gives the compiler exact bounds for "
"`program_id(axis)` / `num_programs(axis)` and makes the grid part of the "
"specialization key (each distinct grid is its own compiled variant). The "
"grid is computed from the output partition (`let grid = z.grid()?`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:427
msgid ""
"let grid = z.grid()?;\n"
"let (z, _x, _y) = gemm(z, x, y)\n"
"    .const_grid(grid)\n"
"    .generics(generics)\n"
"    .sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/04-matrix-multiplication.md:435
msgid ""
"See [`cutile-examples/examples/gemm_static.rs`](https://github.com/NVIDIA/"
"cuda-rust/blob/main/cutile-rs/cutile-examples/examples/gemm_static.rs) for "
"the legacy static example."
msgstr ""

